{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Todoroki Portable Backup\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Save / restore / clean the configuration of a portable REAPER (Windows), for updates ("backup, overwrite the install, restore") and for archives.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Todoroki_Portable Backup}: choose components (All by default) and destination (Temporary for an update, Archive, or any folder)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Todoroki_Portable Restore}: choose a backup and the components to bring back; REAPER closes, files are restored, REAPER relaunches\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Todoroki_Portable Clean backups}: delete old backups\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Todoroki_Portable Clear user data}: empty your personal data before handing the REAPER to someone else (they then restore their own backup)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Also covers RefLab references ({\f1 Data/references}), the RS Trig library ({\f1 Data/RSampler*}) and the {\f1 User} folders of Neural Amp Modeler, Vital and Decent Sampler (folders set with {\b Folders...}, default {\f1 <drive>\\NAM}, {\f1 <drive>\\Vital} and {\f1 <drive>\\DS}).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Toolbar icons are copied into {\f1 Data/toolbar_icons} on first run. Copies run in a PowerShell window (robocopy): REAPER never freezes.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 RefLab - actions and Companion module\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Install together with the {\b RefLab} (JSFX) and {\b Todoroki Companion} packages.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab "Todoroki_RefLab ..." actions: map them to keys or to a MIDI controller\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Companion module: opens {\f1 <REAPER>/Data/references}, keeps the file list up to date and remembers the references of each project\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 RS Trig Kit Builder\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Companion script of the {\b RS Trig Sampler} JSFX (install both packages).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Import .tci files from a Slate Trigger 2 library (one file or a whole folder tree)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Build multi-velocity / round-robin kits from WAV folders\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Everything lands in {\f1 <REAPER>/Data/RSampler}, sorted as Element / Instrument\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab "RS Trig Rescan Library" refreshes the list shown in the sampler's browser\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab "Todoroki_RS Trig TCI Converter.html" (menu: Open TCI converter) does the same TCI import from a web browser, handy for a whole library folder\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pure Lua, no extension required (portable REAPER friendly).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Todoroki Companion\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A single background service shared by the Todoroki scripts and JSFX. It loads {\b modules} ({\f1 Todoroki_Companion_Module_*.lua}) installed by the other packages of the repository, and offers a {\b Lua API} to scripts.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Run the {\b Todoroki_Companion} action (run it again = stop)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Todoroki_Companion autostart (on-off)}: start together with REAPER\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Works with portable REAPER (paths relative to the REAPER folder)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Developer documentation: {\f1 Todoroki_Companion README.md}.\par}
}
